/**
  @page examples-io-mfem Saving and reloading an MFEM field
  @brief Check a mesh and scalar field after a file round trip.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section examples-io-mfem-intro Mesh, space and field

  A finite element field is interpreted through its mesh and finite element
  space. The MFEM mesh file stores the geometry and connectivity; the grid
  function file stores the finite element collection, vector dimension,
  ordering and coefficients.

  This example saves the affine field @f$u(x,y)=x+y@f$ on the unit square,
  reloads both files and evaluates the restored field at cell centroids.
  A scalar @f$P_1@f$ space represents this field exactly up to floating-point
  arithmetic.

  @section examples-io-mfem-builder Construct the mesh

  Four vertices and two triangles describe the square. The explicit builder
  makes the element connectivity visible in this small example.

  @snippet IO/MFEM.cpp mfem-mesh

  @section examples-io-mfem-gf Save and reload the field

  Interpolation supplies the coefficients in the selected space. Save the mesh
  and field as a pair, then construct the restored space on the loaded mesh
  before loading its coefficients.

  @snippet IO/MFEM.cpp mfem-save
  @snippet IO/MFEM.cpp mfem-load

  The check evaluates the restored field through physical points. Its tolerance
  is @f$10^{-12}@f$ for this exactly representable affine field.

  @snippet IO/MFEM.cpp mfem-check

  `Square.xdmf` also exports the restored field for ParaView. Open that file,
  select **Apply**, color by **u** and use **Surface With Edges** to inspect
  the two triangles. The field ranges from zero to two.

  @image html MFEM.png "Restored affine field on the two-triangle mesh."

  @section examples-io-mfem-full Build and run

  Build the `RodinIOMFEM` target and run it in a scratch directory. The program
  writes `Square.mfem.mesh`, `Square.mfem.gf` and the XDMF/HDF5 visualization
  files. It returns `EXIT_FAILURE` if the mesh counts or sampled field values
  fail their checks.

  The complete program is available in @ref IO/MFEM.cpp "MFEM.cpp".

  @section examples-io-mfem-see-also Next steps

  - @ref examples-io-medit "Convert a MEDIT mesh"
  - @ref examples-io-xdmf "Export a time-dependent vector field"
  - @ref guides-io-gridfunctions "Grid-function storage and compatibility"

  @example IO/MFEM.cpp
  @m_examplenavigation{examples-io-mfem,IO/}
  @m_footernavigation
*/
